Parameter:
  (<Article number>)

Description:
  Praises an article in the conference you are currently visiting.
  Praise is a simple way to show appreciation for someone else's
  article.

  If no article number is given, the article you last read is praised.
  If you give an article number, that article in the current conference
  is praised.

  A praised article shows how many people have praised it. The
  conference status also lists praised articles and how many praises
  each one has received.

Observe:
  You cannot praise your own articles, and you can only praise the same
  article once.

  Praise is only available in local conferences, not in your Mailbox,
  Usenet conferences, or FTN conferences.

  Praise is not anonymous. A user's status shows which articles that
  person has praised and when each praise was given.

Background:
  The praise feature was added in October 2025. Internally, praises are
  stored in the conference's extra data under the !(hiss) section.
